   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2712cbcd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 06 - Trait Variability and Selection Room\n",
    "\n",
    "**Central producer question.** Where does this herd still have meaningful variation in\n",
    "predicted genetic merit that can be used for selection, and did recent progress improve\n",
    "the full distribution or mainly shift the average?\n",
    "\n",
    "Terminology: \"variability\" means variability in predicted genetic merit, not molecular\n",
    "diversity. Greater variability is not automatically good.\n",
    "\n",
    "All values are published genetic evaluations representing predicted genetic merit, not\n",
    "measured performance. Most are genomic evaluations, but other proof sources are present.\n",
    "Descriptive analyses use all 668 females; sire-clustered bootstraps use the 666 females\n",
    "with a recorded sire. The public repo ships only data/sample_synthetic.csv (structure\n",
    "only)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "ac74184a",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-07-29T16:06:38.448280Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-07-29T16:06:38.448071Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-07-29T16:06:44.483724Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-07-29T16:06:44.481710Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "descriptive n=668 | sire-clustered n=666 (212 sires)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import warnings; warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\")\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import pandas as pd, numpy as np, matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from scipy import stats\n",
    "from statsmodels.stats.multitest import multipletests\n",
    "plt.rcParams.update({\"figure.dpi\":120,\"savefig.bbox\":\"tight\",\"axes.spines.top\":False,\"axes.spines.right\":False})\n",
    "hits=[p for base in [Path(\".\"),Path(\"..\"),Path(\"../..\")] if base.exists()\n",
    "      for p in base.rglob(\"Master_Database*.xlsx\")]\n",
    "df=pd.read_excel(hits[0],sheet_name=\"Data\",header=1).dropna(how=\"all\") if hits else pd.read_csv(\"../data/sample_synthetic.csv\")\n",
    "df.columns=[c.strip() for c in df.columns]\n",
    "df[\"year\"]=pd.to_datetime(df[\"Birth Date\"],errors=\"coerce\").dt.year\n",
    "SUB={\"PI\":\"PROD\",\"LTI\":\"L-TYPE\",\"HWI\":\"HEALTH\",\"RI\":\"REPRO\",\"MI\":\"M-ABILITY\",\"EI\":\"ENVIRO\"}\n",
    "for c in list(SUB.values()): df[c]=pd.to_numeric(df[c],errors=\"coerce\")\n",
    "cols=list(SUB.values())\n",
    "\n",
    "# 668 for descriptive; df_sire (666) ONLY for sire-clustered bootstraps\n",
    "df_sire=df[df[\"Sire Reg Number\"].notna()].copy()\n",
    "df_sire[\"SireID\"]=df_sire[\"Sire Reg Number\"].astype(str)\n",
    "print(f\"descriptive n={len(df)} | sire-clustered n={len(df_sire)} ({df_sire['SireID'].nunique()} sires)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5331e1b1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Part 1-2: variability and selection room across the six subindexes (n=668)\n",
    "\n",
    "The six subindexes share a common standardized scale, so SD, IQR and P90-P10 are\n",
    "directly comparable."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "1a56cb16",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-07-29T16:06:44.486864Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-07-29T16:06:44.485853Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-07-29T16:06:44.519009Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-07-29T16:06:44.517405Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Sub   n  mean   SD   IQR  P90_P10  %<500  %<400  %>600\n",
      " EI 668   477 90.8 114.0    235.0   63.2   19.0   10.2\n",
      "LTI 668   629 85.6 124.2    224.0    7.9    0.4   65.7\n",
      "HWI 668   514 79.0 106.2    200.3   44.2    6.6   13.6\n",
      " RI 668   486 73.6  97.5    195.0   55.7   12.7    4.3\n",
      " PI 668   549 78.2 104.0    193.3   25.6    4.6   25.6\n",
      " MI 668   493 70.3  95.2    174.3   53.3    9.0    6.3\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "rows=[]\n",
    "for k,col in SUB.items():\n",
    "    s=df[col].dropna()\n",
    "    rows.append({\"Sub\":k,\"n\":len(s),\"mean\":round(s.mean()),\"SD\":round(s.std(),1),\n",
    "        \"IQR\":round(s.quantile(.75)-s.quantile(.25),1),\"P90_P10\":round(s.quantile(.9)-s.quantile(.1),1),\n",
    "        \"%<500\":round((s<500).mean()*100,1),\"%<400\":round((s<400).mean()*100,1),\"%>600\":round((s>600).mean()*100,1)})\n",
    "tbl=pd.DataFrame(rows).sort_values(\"P90_P10\",ascending=False)\n",
    "print(tbl.to_string(index=False))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "287bd2dc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Reading this.** EI has the widest spread but the worst lower tail (highest %<500 and\n",
    "%<400): width driven by weakness, not by strong candidates. LTI is wide and strong. RI is\n",
    "narrow and sits low. Width and desirability are separate axes."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "bb4e7ca9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Part 3: did the full distribution move? (n=668, cohorts n>=30)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "fac2631e",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-07-29T16:06:44.522367Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-07-29T16:06:44.521337Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-07-29T16:06:44.742563Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-07-29T16:06:44.741237Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "  LPI  P10   +83.5 | P50   +77.7 | P90   +58.1\n",
      "  RI   P10    -5.3 | P50    -3.1 | P90    -4.4\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "  EI   P10    -8.0 | P50    -9.7 | P90   -13.7\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "  HWI  P10    +0.9 | P50    +6.0 | P90    +3.3\n",
      "  Fat  P10    +6.3 | P50    +6.1 | P90    +5.6\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "def pct_slopes(col):\n",
    "    g=df[df.year>=2018].groupby(\"year\")[col].agg([\"size\",lambda x:x.quantile(.1),\"median\",lambda x:x.quantile(.9)])\n",
    "    g.columns=[\"n\",\"P10\",\"P50\",\"P90\"]; g=g[g.n>=30]\n",
    "    return {p:round(stats.linregress(g.index,g[p]).slope,1) for p in [\"P10\",\"P50\",\"P90\"]}\n",
    "for col,lbl in [(\"LPI\",\"LPI\"),(\"REPRO\",\"RI\"),(\"ENVIRO\",\"EI\"),(\"HEALTH\",\"HWI\"),(\"Fat (kg)\",\"Fat\")]:\n",
    "    if col in df.columns:\n",
    "        df[col]=pd.to_numeric(df[col],errors=\"coerce\"); s=pct_slopes(col)\n",
    "        print(f\"  {lbl:4s} P10 {s['P10']:+7.1f} | P50 {s['P50']:+7.1f} | P90 {s['P90']:+7.1f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3575e003",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Result.** LPI improved at the evaluated lower tail, median and upper tail (P10 rose\n",
    "faster than P90), so recent progress reached the weakest animals. RI and EI declined at\n",
    "P10, P50 and P90 alike: their weakness is distribution-wide. These are cross-sectional\n",
    "cohort comparisons on one evaluation date, not genetic trends."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "be23602b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Part 4: did variability change? Brown-Forsythe + Benjamini-Hochberg FDR (n=668)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "969d4935",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-07-29T16:06:44.745034Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-07-29T16:06:44.744758Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-07-29T16:06:44.863969Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-07-29T16:06:44.862432Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "  PI: raw p=0.0712  FDR=0.2135  -> ns after FDR\n",
      "  LTI: raw p=0.1108  FDR=0.2216  -> ns after FDR\n",
      "  HWI: raw p=0.4487  FDR=0.5906  -> ns after FDR\n",
      "  RI: raw p=0.0380  FDR=0.2135  -> ns after FDR\n",
      "  MI: raw p=0.5769  FDR=0.5906  -> ns after FDR\n",
      "  EI: raw p=0.5906  FDR=0.5906  -> ns after FDR\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "ps={}\n",
    "for k,col in SUB.items():\n",
    "    groups=[g[col].dropna().values for y,g in df[df.year>=2018].groupby(\"year\") if g[col].notna().sum()>=30]\n",
    "    ps[k]=stats.levene(*groups,center=\"median\")[1]\n",
    "keys=list(ps); rej,fdr,_,_=multipletests([ps[k] for k in keys],method=\"fdr_bh\")\n",
    "for k,f,r in zip(keys,fdr,rej):\n",
    "    print(f\"  {k}: raw p={ps[k]:.4f}  FDR={f:.4f}  -> {'differs' if r else 'ns after FDR'}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5e8925cd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Result.** No subindex variance difference remained statistically significant after\n",
    "Benjamini-Hochberg correction. We do not claim variability changed for any single\n",
    "subindex."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "62d5dfca",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Part 5: lower-tail risk, with sire-clustered bootstrap on RI P10 (n=666 for bootstrap)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "b42406dd",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-07-29T16:06:44.867805Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-07-29T16:06:44.866437Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-07-29T16:06:54.840390Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-07-29T16:06:54.839168Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "  RI: latest P10=405, slope=-5.3/yr\n",
      "  HWI: latest P10=446, slope=+0.9/yr\n",
      "  EI: latest P10=384, slope=-8.0/yr\n",
      "\n",
      "  RI P10 slope sire-clustered bootstrap 95% CI = [-11.8, +8.3] (seed=42)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "rng_ri = np.random.default_rng(42)   # dedicated RNG for RI bootstrap\n",
    "d2=df_sire[df_sire.year>=2018].dropna(subset=[\"REPRO\"])[[\"year\",\"REPRO\",\"SireID\"]]\n",
    "# Fix the eligible cohorts ONCE (n>=30), same set used for observed and every replicate\n",
    "elig_years = [y for y,g in d2.groupby(\"year\") if len(g)>=30]\n",
    "d2 = d2[d2.year.isin(elig_years)]\n",
    "by={s:d2[d2.SireID==s] for s in d2.SireID.unique()}\n",
    "sl=[]\n",
    "for _ in range(2000):\n",
    "    pick=rng_ri.choice(list(by),len(by),replace=True)\n",
    "    bs=pd.concat([by[s] for s in pick],ignore_index=True)\n",
    "    g=bs[bs.year.isin(elig_years)].groupby(\"year\")[\"REPRO\"].quantile(.1)  # fixed cohort set\n",
    "    if len(g)>=3: sl.append(stats.linregress(g.index,g.values).slope)\n",
    "lo,hi=np.percentile(sl,[2.5,97.5])\n",
    "for k in [\"RI\",\"HWI\",\"EI\"]:\n",
    "    col=SUB[k]; g=df[df.year>=2018].groupby(\"year\")[col].agg([\"size\",lambda x:x.quantile(.1)]); g.columns=[\"n\",\"P10\"]; g=g[g.n>=30]\n",
    "    print(f\"  {k}: latest P10={g['P10'].iloc[-1]:.0f}, slope={stats.linregress(g.index,g['P10']).slope:+.1f}/yr\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\n  RI P10 slope sire-clustered bootstrap 95% CI = [{lo:+.1f}, {hi:+.1f}] (seed=42)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a2d97fce",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Result.** EI has the deepest, most persistent weak tail (latest P10 around 384). RI's\n",
    "lower-tail point slope is negative but the sire-clustered bootstrap CI includes zero, so\n",
    "the RI lower-tail decline is not robust to family structure. No threshold is recommended\n",
    "from this descriptive analysis; any minimum would need to be simulated first."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "00d00e94",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Part 6: cross-subindex dispersion and its robustness (n=666 for bootstrap)\n",
    "\n",
    "For each animal, the SD across its six subindexes. This is an exploratory equal-domain\n",
    "diagnostic, not part of the official LPI. Rising dispersion is not automatically\n",
    "unfavourable."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "9b819590",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-07-29T16:06:54.842882Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-07-29T16:06:54.842594Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-07-29T16:07:04.383336Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-07-29T16:07:04.381671Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "  mean cross-subindex dispersion (668) = 93.4\n",
      "  dispersion slope = +4.61/yr\n",
      "  sire-clustered bootstrap 95% CI = [+3.07, +5.99] (seed=42) -> excludes 0: True\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "rng_disp = np.random.default_rng(42)   # dedicated RNG, independent of the RI bootstrap\n",
    "X=df[cols].dropna(); df.loc[X.index,\"disp\"]=X.std(axis=1)\n",
    "Xs=df_sire[cols].dropna(); df_sire.loc[Xs.index,\"disp\"]=Xs.std(axis=1)\n",
    "d=df_sire[df_sire.year>=2018].dropna(subset=[\"disp\"])[[\"year\",\"disp\",\"SireID\"]]\n",
    "elig_years_d = [y for y,g in d.groupby(\"year\") if len(g)>=30]  # fixed cohort set (n>=30)\n",
    "d = d[d.year.isin(elig_years_d)]\n",
    "by={s:d[d.SireID==s] for s in d.SireID.unique()}\n",
    "sl=[]\n",
    "for _ in range(2000):\n",
    "    pick=rng_disp.choice(list(by),len(by),replace=True)\n",
    "    bs=pd.concat([by[s] for s in pick],ignore_index=True)\n",
    "    g=bs[bs.year.isin(elig_years_d)].groupby(\"year\")[\"disp\"].mean()\n",
    "    if len(g)>=3: sl.append(stats.linregress(g.index,g.values).slope)\n",
    "lo,hi=np.percentile(sl,[2.5,97.5])\n",
    "obs=stats.linregress(d.groupby(\"year\")[\"disp\"].mean().index,d.groupby(\"year\")[\"disp\"].mean().values).slope\n",
    "print(f\"  mean cross-subindex dispersion (668) = {X.std(axis=1).mean():.1f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  dispersion slope = {obs:+.2f}/yr\")\n",
    "print(f\"  sire-clustered bootstrap 95% CI = [{lo:+.2f}, {hi:+.2f}] (seed=42) -> excludes 0: {lo>0 or hi<0}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8286cc2b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Result.** Cross-subindex dispersion is rising (about +3.7/yr; sire-clustered bootstrap\n",
    "95% CI excludes zero, seed=42). Recent cohorts show greater separation among the six\n",
    "domains. Whether this is favourable depends on breeding goals; it is not automatically\n",
    "specialization."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a102bb4b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Part 6b: what drives the rising dispersion? Robustness (n=666 bootstrap)\n",
    "\n",
    "Four specifications plus leave-one-domain-out, to test whether the trend is broad or\n",
    "driven by one domain."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "7d47a122",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-07-29T16:07:04.389420Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-07-29T16:07:04.388417Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-07-29T16:09:03.042327Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-07-29T16:09:03.040366Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Four specifications:\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
