   "source": [
    "def disp_trend(cols_use, weights=None, seed=42, reps=2000):\n",
    "    Xu=df[cols_use].dropna()\n",
    "    if weights is None: d0=Xu.std(axis=1)\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        w=np.array(weights)/np.sum(weights); mu=(Xu.values*w).sum(1,keepdims=True)\n",
    "        d0=pd.Series(np.sqrt(((Xu.values-mu)**2*w).sum(1)),index=Xu.index)\n",
    "    tmp=df.loc[Xu.index,[\"year\",\"Sire Reg Number\"]].copy(); tmp[\"disp\"]=d0.values\n",
    "    tmp=tmp[(tmp.year>=2018)&(tmp[\"Sire Reg Number\"].notna())]; tmp[\"SireID\"]=tmp[\"Sire Reg Number\"].astype(str)\n",
    "    ey=[y for y,g in tmp.groupby(\"year\") if len(g)>=30]; tmp=tmp[tmp.year.isin(ey)]  # fixed cohorts n>=30\n",
    "    obs=stats.linregress(tmp.groupby(\"year\")[\"disp\"].mean().index,tmp.groupby(\"year\")[\"disp\"].mean().values).slope\n",
    "    by={s:tmp[tmp.SireID==s] for s in tmp.SireID.unique()}; rng=np.random.default_rng(seed); sl=[]\n",
    "    for _ in range(reps):\n",
    "        pick=rng.choice(list(by),len(by),replace=True); bs=pd.concat([by[s] for s in pick],ignore_index=True)\n",
    "        g=bs[bs.year.isin(ey)].groupby(\"year\")[\"disp\"].mean()\n",
    "        if len(g)>=3: sl.append(stats.linregress(g.index,g.values).slope)\n",
    "    return obs,np.percentile(sl,2.5),np.percentile(sl,97.5)\n",
    "print(\"Four specifications:\")\n",
    "for name,cu,w in [(\"all six\",cols,None),(\"exclude EI\",[c for c in cols if c!=\"ENVIRO\"],None),\n",
    "                  (\"exclude EI+RI\",[c for c in cols if c not in[\"ENVIRO\",\"REPRO\"]],None),\n",
    "                  (\"official LPI weights\",cols,[40,32,8,10,5,5])]:\n",
    "    o,lo,hi=disp_trend(cu,w); print(f\"  {name:22s} slope={o:+.2f} CI=[{lo:+.2f},{hi:+.2f}]\")\n",
    "print(\"\\nLeave-one-domain-out:\")\n",
    "base,_,_=disp_trend(cols); print(f\"  baseline (all six) = {base:+.2f}\")\n",
    "for k,col in SUB.items():\n",
    "    o,lo,hi=disp_trend([c for c in cols if c!=col]); print(f\"  drop {k:4s}: slope={o:+.2f} CI=[{lo:+.2f},{hi:+.2f}]\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1018ce8a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Result.** The trend survives excluding EI (about +4.8) and under the official LPI\n",
    "weights (about +4.5), so it is not an EI artefact or a weighting artefact. But\n",
    "**removing LTI collapses the trend to about zero (CI includes zero)**; no other domain\n",
    "does this. The rising dispersion is driven primarily by L-TYPE increasing faster than the\n",
    "other five domains, not by broad specialization across all domains."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ea72d3d8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Part 7: producer summary\n",
    "\n",
    "\"Where the herd has selection opportunity or lower-tail risk.\" Mean = full-herd mean of\n",
    "predicted merit (n=668)."
   ]
